p data-i="4" aria-hidden="true" class="fact pointer-events-none absolute top-4 left-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-cream py-2 pr-4 pl-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900 shadow-[0_10px_24px_-12px_rgb(0_0_0/0.5)]"><span class="grid size-7 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ghee-400 font-display text-xs">05</span>With a spoon or muslin</p><p data-i="5" aria-hidden="true" class="fact pointer-events-none absolute top-4 left-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-cream py-2 pr-4 pl-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900 shadow-[0_10px_24px_-12px_rgb(0_0_0/0.5)]"><span class="grid size-7 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ghee-400 font-display text-xs">06</span>Cold water wash</p><p data-i="6" aria-hidden="true" class="fact pointer-events-none absolute top-4 left-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-cream py-2 pr-4 pl-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900 shadow-[0_10px_24px_-12px_rgb(0_0_0/0.5)]"><span class="grid size-7 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ghee-400 font-display text-xs">07</span>Nothing added</p><p data-i="7" aria-hidden="true" class="fact pointer-events-none absolute top-4 left-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-cream py-2 pr-4 pl-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-900 shadow-[0_10px_24px_-12px_rgb(0_0_0/0.5)]"><span class="grid size-7 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ghee-400 font-display text-xs">08</span>Cooled for 10 to 15 minutes</p></div></div><ol class="relative mt-4 lg:order-1 lg:mt-0"><span class="absolute top-0 bottom-0 left-[1.4rem] w-[3px] rounded-full bg-pasture-800" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="journey-fill absolute top-0 bottom-0 left-[1.4rem] w-[3px] rounded-full bg-ghee-400" aria-hidden="true"></span><li data-beat="true" class="relative min-h-[40svh] pt-6 pl-16 lg:min-h-[52vh] lg:pt-0"><div class="sticky top-[calc(4rem+3.25rem+42svh)] lg:top-[calc(50vh-6rem)]"><span data-i="0" data-active="" aria-hidden="true" class="bead absolute top-0 -left-16 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-pasture-800 font-display text-base text-pasture-100">01</span><h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-cream sm:text-[2rem]"><span class="sr-only">Step 1: </span>We start with full-fat buffalo milk</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-md text-pasture-100 sm:mt-3 sm:text-lg">Fresh, full-fat milk from our buffaloes. Buffalo milk is naturally thick and rich, which is what makes the ghee creamy and white.</p></div></li><li data-beat="true" class="relative min-h-[40svh] pt-6 pl-16 lg:min-h-[52vh] lg:pt-0"><div class="sticky top-[calc(4rem+3.25rem+42svh)] lg:top-[calc(50vh-6rem)]"><span data-i="1" aria-hidden="true" class="bead absolute top-0 -left-16 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-pasture-800 font-display text-base text-pasture-100">02</span><h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-cream sm:text-[2rem]"><span class="sr-only">Step 2: </span>Heated slowly to a gentle boil</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-md text-pasture-100 sm:mt-3 sm:text-lg">The milk goes into a large pan and is heated slowly to a gentle, rolling boil, stirred now and then so nothing catches at the bottom.</p></div></li><li data-beat="true" class="relative min-h-[40svh] pt-6 pl-16 lg:min-h-[52vh] lg:pt-0"><div class="sticky top-[calc(4rem+3.25rem+42svh)] lg:top-[calc(50vh-6rem)]"><span data-i="2" aria-hidden="true" class="bead absolute top-0 -left-16 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-pasture-800 font-display text-base text-pasture-100">03</span><h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-cream sm:text-[2rem]"><span class="sr-only">Step 3: </span>Covered and left to set</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-md text-pasture-100 sm:mt-3 sm:text-lg">We cover the milk and leave it in a warm, cosy spot for 8 to 12 hours, until it sets into thick dahi.</p></div></li><li data-beat="true" class="relative min-h-[40svh] pt-6 pl-16 lg:min-h-[52vh] lg:pt-0"><div class="sticky top-[calc(4rem+3.25rem+42svh)] lg:top-[calc(50vh-6rem)]"><span data-i="3" aria-hidden="true" class="bead absolute top-0 -left-16 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-pasture-800 font-display text-base text-pasture-100">04</span><h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-cream sm:text-[2rem]"><span class="sr-only">Step 4: </span>Churned the bilona way</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-md text-pasture-100 sm:mt-3 sm:text-lg">The dahi is churned with a wooden madhani, back and forth in the bilona method, until the butter separates.</p></div></li><li data-beat="true" class="relative min-h-[40svh] pt-6 pl-16 lg:min-h-[52vh] lg:pt-0"><div class="sticky top-[calc(4rem+3.25rem+42svh)] lg:top-[calc(50vh-6rem)]"><span data-i="4" aria-hidden="true" class="bead absolute top-0 -left-16 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-pasture-800 font-display text-base text-pasture-100">05</span><h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-cream sm:text-[2rem]"><span class="sr-only">Step 5: </span>The butter, collected by hand</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-md text-pasture-100 sm:mt-3 sm:text-lg">The fresh butter is lifted out carefully with a spoon, or gathered in muslin.</p></div></li><li data-beat="true" class="relative min-h-[40svh] pt-6 pl-16 lg:min-h-[52vh] lg:pt-0"><div class="sticky top-[calc(4rem+3.25rem+42svh)] lg:top-[calc(50vh-6rem)]"><span data-i="5" aria-hidden="true" class="bead absolute top-0 -left-16 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-pasture-800 font-display text-base text-pasture-100">06</span><h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-cream sm:text-[2rem]"><span class="sr-only">Step 6: </span>Washed in cold water</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-md text-pasture-100 sm:mt-3 sm:text-lg">The butter goes into a bowl and is washed with cold water.</p></div></li><li data-beat="true" class="relative min-h-[40svh] pt-6 pl-16 lg:min-h-[52vh] lg:pt-0"><div class="sticky top-[calc(4rem+3.25rem+42svh)] lg:top-[calc(50vh-6rem)]"><span data-i="6" aria-hidden="true" class="bead absolute top-0 -left-16 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-pasture-800 font-display text-base text-pasture-100">07</span><h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-cream sm:text-[2rem]"><span class="sr-only">Step 7: </span>Clarified into ghee</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-md text-pasture-100 sm:mt-3 sm:text-lg">The washed butter is cooked gently until it clarifies into golden ghee, with the rich aroma every Indian kitchen knows.</p></div></li><li data-beat="true" class="relative min-h-[40svh] pt-6 pl-16 lg:min-h-[52vh] lg:pt-0"><div class="sticky top-[calc(4rem+3.25rem+42svh)] lg:top-[calc(50vh-6rem)]"><span data-i="7" aria-hidden="true" class="bead absolute top-0 -left-16 grid size-12 place-items-center rounded-full bg-pasture-800 font-display text-base text-pasture-100">08</span><h3 class="font-display text-2xl leading-tight text-cream sm:text-[2rem]"><span class="sr-only">Step 8: </span>Cooled, then strained through muslin</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-md text-pasture-100 sm:mt-3 sm:text-lg">Finally the ghee cools for 10 to 15 minutes and is strained through muslin into the jar. No preservatives, no additives.</p></div></li></ol></div><div class="wrap flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 pb-16 lg:pb-24"><a class="btn btn-gold text-lg" href="/products/pure-desi-buffalo-ghee">Shop ghee</a><span class="ml-2 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-pasture-200"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 20" class="h-4 w-3.5 text-ghee-400" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 1C10 5 15 9 15 13a7 7 0 0 1-14 0C1 9 6 5 8 1Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg>No preservatives, no additives, ever</span></div></section>
<section class="bg-oat" aria-labelledby="vs"><div class="wrap grid gap-8 py-14 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] lg:gap-10 lg:py-20"><div><div class="max-w-3xl "><h2 id="vs" class="font-display leading-[1.04] text-balance text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-900">Buffalo ghee or cow ghee?</h2></div><p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-800">Both are good ghee. Buffalo ghee is whiter, thicker and richer, and is the choice for many traditional sweets and fried food.</p><a class="link mt-6 inline-block" href="/blogs/know-your-ghee/buffalo-ghee-vs-cow-ghee">Read the full comparison</a></div><div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-[1.5rem] bg-milk p-1.5 shadow-[0_1px_0_var(--color-line),0_24px_50px_-34px_rgb(35_27_30/0.4)]"><table class="table-ghee"><caption class="sr-only">Buffalo ghee compared with cow ghee</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col" class="w-[24%]"><span class="sr-only">Attribute</span></th><th scope="col" class="rounded-t-xl bg-ghee-100">Buffalo ghee</th><th scope="col">Cow ghee</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Colour</th><td class="bg-ghee-100 font-medium ">Creamy white</td><td class="text-ink-700">Golden yellow</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Why the colour</th><td class="bg-ghee-100 font-medium ">Buffalo milk has almost no beta-carotene</td><td class="text-ink-700">Cow milk carries beta-carotene from fodder</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Fat in the milk</th><td class="bg-ghee-100 font-medium ">About 6 to 8%</td><td class="text-ink-700">About 3.5 to 4.5%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Texture</th><td class="bg-ghee-100 font-medium ">Thick and creamy, sets firm when cool</td><td class="text-ink-700">Softer, often grainy</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Taste</th><td class="bg-ghee-100 font-medium ">Rich and sweet</td><td class="text-ink-700">Lighter and nutty</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Best for</th><td class="bg-ghee-100 font-medium rounded-b-xl">Halwa, ladoo, mithai, parathas, puris and frying</td><td class="text-ink-700">Everyday tadka, dal and rice</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
<section class="py-14 lg:py-20" aria-labelledby="process-faq"><div class="wrap grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]"><div><div class="max-w-3xl "><h2 id="process-faq" class="font-display leading-[1.04] text-balance text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-ink-900">Questions about how it is made</h2></div><a class="btn btn-ink mt-8" href="/products/pure-desi-buffalo-ghee">Shop buffalo ghee</a></div><div class="divide-y divide-line border-y border-line"><details name="faq" class="group"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-5 [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><h3 class="text-lg leading-snug font-semibold">What is the bilona method?</h3><span class="mt-1 shrink-0 rounded-full border border-ink-200 p-1 transition-transform group-open:rotate-45"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="size-4" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="max-w-[68ch] pb-6 text-ink-800">Milk is heated, set into dahi, and the dahi is churned with a wooden madhani until butter separates. The butter is then clarified into ghee. Farm Dip follows this method with full-fat buffalo milk.</p></details><details name="faq" class="group"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-5 [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><h3 class="text-lg leading-snug font-semibold">How long does the milk take to set?</h3><span class="mt-1 shrink-0 rounded-full border border-ink-200 p-1 transition-transform group-open:rotate-45"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="size-4" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="max-w-[68ch] pb-6 text-ink-800">After a slow boil, the milk is covered and left in a warm, cosy spot for 8 to 12 hours until it sets into dahi.</p></details><details name="faq" class="group"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-5 [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><h3 class="text-lg leading-snug font-semibold">Why is the butter washed in cold water?</h3><span class="mt-1 shrink-0 rounded-full border border-ink-200 p-1 transition-transform group-open:rotate-45"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="size-4" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="max-w-[68ch] pb-6 text-ink-800">Washing the fresh butter in cold water rinses away the buttermilk (chhaach) that clings to it before it is clarified into ghee.</p></details><details name="faq" class="group"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-5 [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><h3 class="text-lg leading-snug font-semibold">Is anything added to Farm Dip ghee?</h3><span class="mt-1 shrink-0 rounded-full border border-ink-200 p-1 transition-transform group-open:rotate-45"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="size-4" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="max-w-[68ch] pb-6 text-ink-800">No. There are no preservatives, no additives and no colour. It is ghee made from pure buffalo milk.</p></details></div></div></section>

